exit|PASS: Way-out noun, leaving a hall and closing a program are distinct; save-before-exit preserves the separation of actions and noun/verb constructions are source supported.
mist|PASS: Fine suspended droplets and still-visible far bank distinguish light mist from dense fog; layer-of and generally-lighter qualification avoid an absolute weather threshold.
raisin|PASS: Dried grape is accurate and not confused with a fresh variety; oat-biscuit example and handful quantity translate naturally with countable fruit grammar.
ton|REVIEW: [SEMANTICS] Multiple measurement systems remain explicitly unresolved in the cargo example; no exact conversion or claim that every ton equals a metric tonne is introduced.
wicked|REVIEW: [SENSE_BOUNDARY] Cruel moral adjective is accurately illustrated by a fictional ruler; other colloquial or playful uses remain outside this source-limited draft and require coverage review.
